      "body": "<!--\nNote: bpftrace is under active development and not all distros ship the most\nrecent version yet. Please make sure the bug reproduces on the latest release\nor master.\n-->\n\n### What reproduces the bug? Provide code if possible.\n\nhttps://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/blob/master/INSTALL.md does not mention the need for a static libbpf. At least on Arch Linux there is *no* package that provides a libbpf (only a shared library is available), so you end up having to build your own libbpf, which is really not ideal.\n\nAt the very least the install instructions should be updated with this huge gotcha, but it would be better to not depend on linking statically.\n\nAdditionally the error message is completely incorrect: `Please install the libbpf development package (missing: LIBBPF_LIBRARIES)` does not help, as:\n\n1. Arch does not use separated -dev packages. Headers are included in the main package for every package.\n2. No dev package with a static linking exists.\n\nA better error message should mention specifically the lack of `libbpf.a` instead of requiring the user to dig through the cmake files to figure out what on earth the error is talking about.\n\n### `bpftrace --info` output\n\nN/A. Git version is 815073672a277f23ce04e70a1ae28ca980072b7b",
