      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "Our current release assets are a bit messy. Take for example https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/releases/tag/v0.22.1. We upload:\n\n* binary_tools_man-bundle.tar.xz\n* binary_tools_man-bundle.tar.zst\n* bpftrace\n* man.tar.xz\n* tools-with-help.tar.xz\n* tools.tar.xz\n\nThe intent was to pre-package some popular combinations. That was nice for a time, but now we want to add aarch64 artifacts (https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/2868). In the future, possibly even more. If we are to continue with current scheme, we'd be unnecessarily multiplying number of artifacts.\n\nLet's simplify. I propose:\n* Remove combinations. Just let users pick and choose what they want.\n  * It's also more flexible.\n* Remove multiple compression options and stick to zstd.\n  * Originally in 2021 zstd was not as popular so we mainly used xz, but 4 years later and the entire internet is standardizing around zstd.\n* Suffix bpftrace binary with architecture\n\nUnder new scheme (with additional aarch64), the artifacts would be:\n* bpftrace.x86-64\n* bpftrace.aarch64\n* man.tar.zst\n* tools.tar.zst\n* tools-help.tar.zst\n\nNote the suffix change from `zstd` -> `zst`. `zst` is the extension as documented by [RFC 8878](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8878).\n\nAlso note we don't compress the appimage binaries. Appimage already does compression.",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/3739/reactions",
