      "type": {
        "id": 82713,
        "node_id": "IT_kwDOCWTeF84AAUMZ",
        "name": "Feature",
        "description": "A request, idea, or new functionality",
        "color": "blue",
        "created_at": "2024-01-24T13:01:17Z",
        "updated_at": "2024-10-08T08:29:56Z",
        "is_enabled": true
      },
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "sub_issues_summary": {
        "total": 0,
        "completed": 0,
        "percent_completed": 0
      },
      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "For USDT, there are builtin variables `arg0`, `arg1`, ..., `argN`. - Arguments to the traced function; assumed to be 64 bits wide.\r\nBut if we want to trace multiple USDTs together, and each of them has different number of argements, it is very difficult to write the bpftrace script.\r\nWe have to list each USDT seperatly but with duplicate entries, because we have no signal on how many arguements it actually has.\r\nAnd `arg0`, `arg1`, ... are tested statically during compilation, so not possible to workaround it, e.g. save the number of arguements as `arg0`, then iterate `arg1`, `arg2` ... under the hint of `arg0`.\r\n\r\nSample:\r\n```\r\nTRACE0(TRACE, TEST0);\r\nTRACE1(TRACE, TEST1, 1); \r\n```\r\n```\r\nusdt:xxx.TRACE.TEST0,\r\nusdt.xxx.TRACE.TEST1\r\n{\r\n  printf(\"%d\\n\", arg0);    <- compile error: \"couldn't get argument 0\"\r\n}\r\n```",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/1349/reactions",
        "total_count": 1,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
