        "percent_completed": 0
      },
      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.\n\nCurrently, including C headers which include typedefs are not handled properly by bpftrace; in some cases, it's possible to use them, but you have to add `struct` before them, and in other cases, the type itself simply isn't recognized. By \"not recognized,\" I mean that `SemanticAnalyser::resolve_struct_type` throws an error.\n\n### Describe the solution you'd like\n\nCurrently, it appears as if `ClangParser::visit_children` should simply handle the case where `clang_getCursorKind(c) == CXCursor_TypedefDecl`. If it sees a `typedef` for a particular struct, it should add it to the `structs` map, like all other structs. This seems to be the simplest way to fix this, but ignores other types that are `typedef`d.\n\n### Describe alternative solutions or features you've considered\n\nProperly keeping track of new types (apart from structs specifically) seems like the correct solution. We could have a new map of types, exactly like the `structs` map.",
      "reactions": {
