      "type": {
        "id": 82712,
        "node_id": "IT_kwDOCWTeF84AAUMY",
        "name": "Bug",
        "description": "An unexpected problem or behavior",
        "color": "red",
        "created_at": "2024-01-24T13:01:17Z",
        "updated_at": "2024-07-26T10:04:48Z",
        "is_enabled": true
      },
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "sub_issues_summary": {
        "total": 0,
        "completed": 0,
        "percent_completed": 0
      },
      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "<!--\nNote: bpftrace is under active development and not all distros ship the most\nrecent version yet. Please make sure the bug reproduces on the latest release\nor master.\n-->\n\ncc: @danobi @anakryiko\n\n### What reproduces the bug? Provide code if possible.\n\nConsider the following program that uses [USDT library](https://github.com/libbpf/usdt):\n```C\n#include \"usdt.h\"\n\n#define __weak __attribute__((weak))\n#define __optimize __attribute__((optimize(2)))\n\nstruct st_regpair { long x, y; };\n\n__weak __optimize void fn_struct_by_val_reg_pair(struct st_regpair a)\n{\n\tUSDT(test, struct_by_val_reg_pair, a);\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv)\n{\n\tstruct st_regpair s = { 3, 4 };\n\tfn_struct_by_val_reg_pair(s);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n```\n\nAnd the following bpftrace script:\n```\nBEGIN { printf(\"STARTED!\\n\"); }\nU:./a.out:test:struct_by_val_reg_pair { printf(\"test:struct_by_val_reg_pair: s.x=%llx\\n\", arg0); }\nEND { printf(\"DONE!\\n\"); }\n```\n\nWhen compiled with gcc, bpftrace captures the trace as expected:\n```shell\n$ cc --version | grep cc\ncc (GCC) 14.2.1 20240912 (Red Hat 14.2.1-3)\n\n$ cc -g program.c\n\n$ sudo ./bpftrace -v -c a.out script.bt \nAST node count: 20\nAttaching 3 probes...\nSTARTED!\ntest:struct_by_val_reg_pair: s.x=3\nDONE!\n```\n\nHowever, when user program is compiled with clang, bpftrace fails with BPF verifier error:\n```shell\n$ clang --version | grep version\nclang version 18.1.8 (Fedora 18.1.8-1.fc40)\n\n$ clang -g program.c\n\n$ sudo ./bpftrace -v -c a.out script.bt \nAST node count: 20\nAttaching 3 probes...\nERROR: Error loading BPF program for BEGIN_1.\nKernel error log: \nprocessed 23 insns (limit 1000000) max_states_per_insn 0 total_states 1 peak_states 1 mark_read 1\n\n\nERROR: Error loading BPF program for usdt___a_out_test_struct_by_val_reg_pair_loc0_2.\nKernel error log: \n0: R1=ctx() R10=fp0\n;  @ bpftrace.bpf.o:0\n0: (b7) r2 = 1                        ; R2_w=1\n1: (7b) *(u64 *)(r10 -24) = r2        ; R2_w=1 R10=fp0 fp-24_w=1\n2: (79) r3 = *(u64 *)(r1 +32)         ; R1=ctx() R3_w=scalar()\n3: (07) r3 += -16                     ; R3_w=scalar()\n4: (bf) r1 = r10                      ; R1_w=fp0 R10=fp0\n5: (07) r1 += -8                      ; R1_w=fp-8\n6: (b7) r2 = 16                       ; R2_w=16\n7: (85) call bpf_probe_read_user#112\ninvalid indirect access to stack R1 off=-8 size=16\nprocessed 8 insns (limit 1000000) max_states_per_insn 0 total_states 0 peak_states 0 mark_read 0\n\nERROR: Loading BPF object(s) failed.\n```\n\nWhen running on arm64 (using an [arm64 bpftrace appimage](https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/actions/runs/13335662074)), tracing similar USDT in gcc-compiled program [fails with a different error](https://github.com/libbpf/usdt/actions/runs/13338018288/job/37257298885):\n```\nParse error:\n    16@x0\n----^\nParse error:\n    24@[x0]\n----^\n\n   [...]\n\nParse error:\n    16@x0\n----^\nParse error:\n    24@[x0]\n----^\nERROR: couldn't get argument 0 for .output/static/arg_types:test:struct_by_val_reg_pair\n```\n\n### `bpftrace --info` output\n```\nSystem\n  OS: Linux 6.12.11-100.fc40.x86_64 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu Jan 23 22:07:15 UTC 2025\n  Arch: x86_64\n\nBuild\n  version: v0.22.1\n  LLVM: 19.1.4\n  bfd: yes\n  liblldb (DWARF support): yes\n  libsystemd (systemd notify support): no\n\nKernel helpers\n  probe_read: yes                  probe_read_str: yes                \n  probe_read_user: yes             probe_read_user_str: yes           \n  probe_read_kernel: yes           probe_read_kernel_str: yes         \n  get_current_cgroup_id: yes       send_signal: yes                   \n  override_return: no              get_boot_ns: yes                   \n  dpath: no                        skboutput: no                      \n  get_tai_ns: yes                  get_func_ip: yes                   \n  jiffies64: yes                   for_each_map_elem: yes             \n\nKernel features\n  Instruction limit: 1000000       Loop support: yes                  \n  btf: yes                         module btf: yes                    \n  Kernel DWARF: no                 map batch: yes                     \n  uprobe refcount: yes             \n\nMap types                          \n  hash: yes                        array: yes                         \n  percpu array: yes                stack_trace: yes                   \n  perf_event_array: yes            ringbuf: yes                       \n\nProbe types\n  kprobe: yes                      tracepoint: yes                    \n  perf_event: yes                  fentry: yes                        \n  kprobe_multi: yes                uprobe_multi: yes                  \n  iter: yes                   \n```",
