      "body": "Fixes #3473.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nWhen BTF is enabled, `ClangParser` defines `_LINUX_TYPES_H` so kernel types can\r\ncome from BTF. At the same time, `/bpftrace/include` was passed as an\r\n`-isystem` directory. Clang could therefore select an incomplete system\r\n`linux/types.h` instead of bpftrace's UAPI-compatible copy, leading to missing\r\ntypes such as `__aligned_u64` when a user supplied kernel or transitive system\r\nheader.\r\n\r\nPrioritizing `/bpftrace/include` exposed two related C-header problems:\r\n\r\n- bpftrace's embedded `stdint.h` and `limits.h` reused Clang's\r\n  `__CLANG_*` include guards. Their `#include_next` entered Clang's copy after\r\n  already defining the same guard, so Clang skipped its header and types or\r\n  macros disappeared.\r\n- Standard macros such as `UINTPTR_MAX` contain valid uppercase integer\r\n  suffixes such as `UL`, while `util::to_uint()` only accepted lowercase\r\n  suffixes.\r\n\r\nAn earlier revision removed the embedded headers and added `clang-unwrapped`\r\nto the Nix environment. Rechecking that approach showed that it created a\r\nruntime dependency on compiler resource headers, still failed `limits.h` on\r\nthe LLVM 18–20 Nix jobs, and interfered with the Nix compiler wrapper in an\r\nLLVM 22 Clang build.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n- Pass only `/bpftrace/include` as `-I`, ensuring that bpftrace's compatibility\r\n  headers take precedence.\r\n- Keep discovered system and architecture directories as `-isystem`.\r\n- Retain the embedded `stdint.h` and `limits.h`, but give them\r\n  bpftrace-specific include guards so `#include_next` can enter Clang's copy.\r\n- Provide a `UINTPTR_MAX` spelling that also works with LLVM 18's detailed\r\n  preprocessing record.\r\n- Accept uppercase `U`/`L` C integer suffixes while leaving bpftrace time-unit\r\n  suffixes case-sensitive.\r\n- Try `clang-<LLVM major>` and then unversioned `clang` when discovering system\r\n  include directories. Success is tracked independently for each attempt.\r\n- Add parser and runtime coverage for the kernel-header path, standard-header\r\n  macros, and environments where no Clang executable is available at runtime.\r\n\r\nThis keeps bpftrace usable in packaged or minimal environments without making\r\na Clang executable a mandatory runtime dependency.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\nI first checked the rebased upstream revision without this patch:\r\n\r\n- Debian Sid, LLVM 21: `linux/sched.h` parses on the current 6.12 kernel, but\r\n  `UINTPTR_MAX` is unknown and `UINT_MAX` cannot be expanded.\r\n- Fedora Rawhide, LLVM 22: the Infiniband reproduction still fails while\r\n  parsing `infiniband/verbs.h`, with missing `uint8_t`, `uint32_t`, and\r\n  `uint64_t`.\r\n\r\nThe updated patch was then tested as follows:\r\n\r\n| Environment | Result |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| Nix, LLVM 18.1.8 | Build passes; `stdint.h` and `limits.h` pass with normal `PATH` and `PATH=/nonexistent` |\r\n| Debian Sid, LLVM 21.1.8 | Focused runtime suite passes 5/5 |\r\n| Fedora Rawhide, LLVM 22.1.8 | `linux/sched.h`, `stdint.h`, `limits.h`, and `infiniband/verbs.h` pass with normal `PATH` and `PATH=/nonexistent` |\r\n| Parser/Clang unit coverage | New uppercase-suffix tests and all Clang parser tests pass |\r\n| Formatting | `git clang-format --diff upstream/master` reports no changes; `git diff --check` passes |\r\n\r\nThe full local unit run passed 979/980 tests. The only failure was\r\n`pid_filter_pass.no_add_filter`, which is unrelated to the changed files and\r\npassed twice when rerun independently.\r\n\r\nThe previously requested `tests/codegen-tests.sh` command exits successfully.\r\nUpstream removed the codegen test suite in November 2025, so the script now\r\nonly reports that those tests are deprecated and no longer exist.\r\n\r\nThe exact Debian 10/custom 5.4 kernel environment from #3473 was not recreated.\r\nThe later Infiniband reproduction documented on this PR was reproduced against\r\ncurrent upstream and passes with this patch.\r\n\r\n##### Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Language changes are updated in `docs/language.md`, `docs/stdlib.md`, or `man/adoc/bpftrace.adoc` (not applicable: this fixes compatibility with valid C macro syntax rather than adding a new language feature)\r\n- [x] User-visible and non-trivial changes updated in `CHANGELOG.md`\r\n- [x] The new behaviour is covered by tests",
      "reactions": {
