      "body": "<!--\nNote: bpftrace is under active development and not all distros ship the most\nrecent version yet. Please make sure the bug reproduces on the latest release\nor master.\n-->\n\n### ERROR: Unable to attach probe: kprobe:fuse:fuse_open.\n```bash\n$ ./bpftrace -ve 'kprobe:fuse:fuse_open {printf(\"%s\", kstack);}'\nTrying to attach probe: kprobe:fuse:fuse_open\nERROR: Unable to attach probe: kprobe:fuse:fuse_open. If this is expected, set the 'missing_probes' config variable to 'warn'.\n```\n\nAfter commit https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/commit/60242629 , bpftrace can't use \"kprobe:[module]:[function]\"\n",
