      "locked": false,
      "assignees": [

      ],
      "milestone": null,
      "comments": 4,
      "created_at": "2025-10-24T08:05:22Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-13T14:44:20Z",
      "closed_at": "2025-10-30T16:28:13Z",
      "assignee": null,
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": null,
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "draft": false,
      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4766",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4766",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4766.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4766.patch",
        "merged_at": "2025-10-30T16:28:13Z"
      },
      "body": "Currently, the `TracepointFormatParser` class is just a collection of static functions. Some of them are called by `ParseTracepointFormatPass` and implement the actual pass, others are called by other passes for, e.g., getting a name of the structure type containing the parsed argument types.\r\n\r\nThis architecture is quite cumbersome and doesn't fit our pass infrastructure so refactor `TracepointFormatParser` to a nicer structure:\r\n\r\n- The `TracepointFormatParser` is now a proper class which contains methods to open and parse a tracepoint format file. It is expected that one instance of `TracepointFormatParser` is created per tracepoint.\r\n\r\n- For failures (e.g. tracepoint format file doesn't exist), methods of `TracepointFormatParser` return new `TracepointFormatFileError`.\r\n\r\n- The pass is implemented using a new `TracepointArgsResolver` visitor.\r\n\r\nThis should preserve the original behavior.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease provide a description of your change below this comment.\r\n\r\nThen please complete the checklist.\r\n\r\nUseful contribution guidelines and tips are in docs/developers.md.\r\n\r\nWarning: please make sure that you have implemented and tested your\r\n         change against the latest version of bpftrace (unless opening a\r\n         PR for a release branch).\r\n-->\r\n\r\n##### Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Language changes are updated in `docs/language.md`, `docs/stdlib.md`, or `man/adoc/bpftrace.adoc`\r\n- [ ] User-visible and non-trivial changes updated in `CHANGELOG.md`\r\n- [ ] The new behaviour is covered by tests\r\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4766/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
