      "type": null,
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "draft": false,
      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4978",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4978",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4978.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4978.patch",
        "merged_at": "2026-02-07T18:16:58Z"
      },
      "body": "Stacked PRs:\n * #4980\n * #4979\n * __->__#4978\n\n\n--- --- ---\n\n### async: remove exceptions from async handlers\n\n\nInstead, use regular error propagation. The program can keep running\nwhen a \"FatalUserException\" has occured, which may be for many reasons.\nThis also simplifies testing, which no longer requires stderr capture.\n\nSigned-off-by: Adin Scannell <amscanne@meta.com>\n",
      "reactions": {
