      "body": "<!--\nNote: bpftrace is under active development and not all distros ship the most\nrecent version yet. Please make sure the bug reproduces on the latest release\nor master.\n-->\n\n### What reproduces the bug? Provide code if possible.\nWhile rebuilding 0.25.1 3 test failures are found which previously passed ok.\n\n### `bpftrace --info` output\n```\n++ tests/runtime-tests.sh\n====================\nbpftrace --info:\n====================\nSystem\n  OS: Linux 7.0.5-7.0-alt1 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri May  8 09:01:47 UTC 2026\n  Arch: x86_64\n\nBuild\n  version: v0.25.1\n  LLVM: 19.1.7\n  bfd: yes\n  libdw (DWARF support): yes\n  libsystemd (systemd notify support): no\n  blazesym (advanced symbolization): no\n\nKernel helpers\n  dpath: yes                       get_tai_ns: yes\n  get_func_ip: yes                 lookup_percpu_elem: yes\n\nKernel features\n  Instruction limit: 1000000       btf: yes\n  module btf: yes                  map batch: yes\n\nProbe types\n  kprobe_multi: yes                uprobe_multi: yes\n  kprobe_session: yes              iter: yes\n```\n```\n[ RUN      ] basic.it lists misc in verbose mode\n[  FAILED  ] basic.it lists misc in verbose mode (643 ms)\n        Command: /usr/src/RPM/BUILD/bpftrace-0.25.1/x86_64-alt-linux/tests/../src/bpftrace --verify-llvm-ir -lv 'kprobe:vfs_read,struct file'\n        Expected: struct file {\n        Found:\nkprobe:vfs_read\\n    struct file * arg0\\n    char * arg1\\n    size_t arg2\\n    loff_t * arg3\\n\n```\n```\n[  FAILED  ] basic.it lists multiple struct definitions (854 ms)\n        Command: /usr/src/RPM/BUILD/bpftrace-0.25.1/x86_64-alt-linux/tests/../src/bpftrace --verify-llvm-ir -lv 'struct task_struct,struct file,struct fd'\n        Expected: struct file {\n        Found:\nstruct task_struct {\\n\\tstruct thread_info thread_info;\\n\\tunsigned int __state;\\n\\tunsigned int saved_state;\\n\\tvoid *stack;\\n\\trefcount_t usage;\\n\\tunsigned int flags;\\n\\tunsigned int ptrace;\\n\\ti