        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4462",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4462",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4462.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4462.patch",
        "merged_at": "2025-08-27T19:35:20Z"
      },
      "body": "Stacked PRs:\n * __->__#4462\n\n\n--- --- ---\n\n### semantics: add `fail` function to the SemanicAnalyser\n\n\nThis allows for compilation failure in non-pruned paths. For example,\nconsider a `static_assert` macro:\n\n```\nmacro static_assert(v, msg) {\n  if (typeof(v) != typeof(true)) {\n    fail(\"unable to evaluate compile-time assert\");\n  } else if (!v) {\n    fail(msg);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSigned-off-by: Adin Scannell <amscanne@meta.com>\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4462/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
