      "number": 4418,
      "title": "macros: expand literals as literals",
      "user": {
        "login": "amscanne",
        "id": 425773,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTc3Mw==",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/425773?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/amscanne",
        "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/followers",
        "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/following{/other_user}",
        "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/gists{/gist_id}",
        "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
        "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/subscriptions",
        "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/orgs",
        "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/repos",
        "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/events{/privacy}",
        "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/received_events",
        "type": "User",
        "user_view_type": "public",
        "site_admin": false
      },
      "labels": [

      ],
      "state": "closed",
      "locked": false,
      "assignees": [

      ],
      "milestone": null,
      "comments": 1,
      "created_at": "2025-07-30T21:57:46Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-08-28T04:55:40Z",
      "closed_at": "2025-08-28T04:55:40Z",
      "assignee": null,
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": null,
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "draft": true,
      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4418",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4418",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4418.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4418.patch",
        "merged_at": null
      },
      "body": "Stacked PRs:\n * __->__#4418\n * #4417\n * #4401\n * #4416\n\n\n--- --- ---\n\n### macros: expand literals as literals\n\n\nCurrently we will assign literals to a temporary variable during\nexpansion. This may result in some type marshalling and an inability to\nfold properly. This change allows literals to expand as literals, and\nalso ensures that they are not mutated (just like expressions\npreviously). Since they expand as literals, they will continue to be\nfolded during expansion.\n\nIn order to allow literals to be recursively folding, it was necessary\nto pull folding ahead of expansion. The only problem with this is that\npositional parameters are also folded. Therefore, we run a portability\ncheck before and after parsing: first will capture positional\nparameters, and afterwards will capture the use of any builtins, etc.\nthat may be non-portable.\n\nWith this in place, we can trivally support the creation of a\n`static_assert` macro, which works as expected. It is mostly useful for\n`sizeof`, `offsetof`, `typeof` and similar functions.\n\n```\nbegin {\n static_assert(1 > 0, \"the world is upside down\");\n static_assert(1 < 0, \"the world is okay\");\n}\n```\n\nSigned-off-by: Adin Scannell <amscanne@meta.com>\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4418/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
        "laugh": 0,
        "hooray": 0,
        "confused": 0,
