      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "### What reproduces the bug? Provide code if possible.\n\nRunning the following test program with a current Github Actions artifact of bpftrace on arm64 (see below for `bpftrace --info` output)...\n\n```\ntracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_exec*\n{\n        printf(\"%p %s\\n\", args->filename, str(uptr(args->filename)));\n}\n```\n\n... and repeatedly calling `/bin/false` yields the following output:\n```\n./bpftrace exectest\nAttached 2 probes\n0x556f762960\n0x556f890640\n0x556f89e1d0\n0x556f75f990\n0x556f895350 /bin/false\n0x556f762a90 /bin/false\n0x556f7628b0\n0x556f8607b0\n0x556f7db060\n0x556f7f2970\n0x556f762960 /bin/false\n0x556f760cd0 /bin/false\n0x556f760b30\n0x556f8312f0\n0x556f82bc80\n0x556f760c30 /bin/false\n0x556f7765c0\n```\n\nMore often than not, bpftrace fails to print the filename. It seems to be working or failing at random. (`/bin/false` was just chosen as an example, it happens with any exec'ed binary.)\n\nRunning `bpftrace -k` prints the following error:\n```\n./bpftrace -k exectest\nAttached 2 probes\nexectest:21:36-61: WARNING: Bad address\nAdditional Info - helper: probe_read_user_str, retcode: -14\n    printf(\"%p %s\\n\", args->filename, str(uptr(args->filename)));\n                                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nexectest:20-22: WARNING: expanded from\n{\n        printf(\"%p %s\\n\", args->filename, str(uptr(args->filename)));\n}\n0x556f89c0a0\n```\n\n### `bpftrace --info` output\n\n```\n./bpftrace  --info\nSystem\n  OS: Linux 6.12.47+rpt-rpi-v8 #1 SMP PREEMPT Debian 1:6.12.47-1+rpt1~bookworm (2025-09-16)\n  Arch: aarch64\n\nBuild\n  version: v0.24.0\n  LLVM: 21.1.0\n  bfd: yes\n  libdw (DWARF support): yes\n  libsystemd (systemd notify support): yes\n  blazesym (advanced symbolization): yes\n\nlibbpf: kernel BTF is missing at '/sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux', was CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF enabled?\nlibbpf: failed to find valid kernel BTF\nKernel helpers\n  dpath: no                        get_tai_ns: yes\n  get_func_ip: yes                 lookup_percpu_elem: yes\n\nKernel features\n  Instruction limit: 1000000       btf: no\n  module btf: no                   map batch: yes\n\nProbe types\n  kprobe_multi: no                 uprobe_multi: no\n  kprobe_session: no               iter: no\n```\n(Static ARM64 binary was taken from this run: https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/actions/runs/18409583799)\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4717/reactions",
