      "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4959",
      "id": 3830652606,
      "node_id": "PR_kwDOCMCh9c6-Do_Z",
      "number": 4959,
      "title": "Speed up probes listing ",
      "user": {
        "login": "sgruszka",
        "id": 1064254,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjQyNTQ=",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1064254?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/sgruszka",
        "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/followers",
        "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/following{/other_user}",
        "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/gists{/gist_id}",
        "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
        "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/subscriptions",
        "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/orgs",
        "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/repos",
        "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/events{/privacy}",
        "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sgruszka/received_events",
        "type": "User",
        "user_view_type": "public",
        "site_admin": false
      },
      "labels": [

      ],
      "state": "closed",
      "locked": false,
      "assignees": [

      ],
      "milestone": null,
      "comments": 1,
      "created_at": "2026-01-19T17:36:10Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-01-28T10:51:14Z",
      "closed_at": "2026-01-28T10:51:14Z",
      "assignee": null,
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": null,
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "draft": false,
      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4959",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4959",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4959.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4959.patch",
        "merged_at": "2026-01-28T10:51:14Z"
      },
      "body": "Do speedup of probe listing/matching based on observation, that reading whole `available_filter_functions` is slow as it has to dynamically resolve ksymbols for modules. Reading part of file that contains only vmlinux symbols is fast:\r\n```\r\nroot@nano:~# time cat /sys/kernel/tracing/available_filter_functions | wc -l\r\n73041\r\n\r\nreal\t0m1.228s\r\nuser\t0m0.000s\r\nsys\t0m1.224s\r\nroot@nano:~# time awk '\r\n{\r\n    if ($0 ~ /\\[[A-Za-z]+\\]$/)\r\n        exit\r\n    count++\r\n}\r\n\r\nEND {\r\n    print count\r\n}' /sys/kernel/tracing/available_filter_functions\r\n50363\r\n\r\nreal\t0m0.077s\r\nuser\t0m0.007s\r\nsys\t0m0.069s\r\n\r\n```\r\nWe can lazy read the `available_filter_functions` and also search only for functions belonging to particular module, if we have information about used module. That will make listing/matching probes faster in various scenarios.\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n```\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -l   | wc -l\r\n147441\r\n\r\nreal\t0m3.557s\r\nuser\t0m0.744s\r\nsys\t0m2.868s\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -l  \"fentry:*\"  | wc -l\r\n70785\r\n\r\nreal\t0m2.015s\r\nuser\t0m0.512s\r\nsys\t0m1.526s\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -l  \"fentry:vmlinux:*\"  | wc -l\r\n48605\r\n\r\nreal\t0m1.783s\r\nuser\t0m0.384s\r\nsys\t0m1.418s\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -e  'fentry:vmlinux:schedule { print(comm) ; exit(0) }'\r\nAttached 1 probe\r\nbpftrace\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nreal\t0m2.103s\r\nuser\t0m0.396s\r\nsys\t0m1.454s\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter :\r\n\r\n```\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -l   | wc -l\r\n147439\r\n\r\nreal\t0m2.190s\r\nuser\t0m0.773s\r\nsys\t0m1.483s\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -l  \"fentry:*\"  | wc -l\r\n70783\r\n\r\nreal\t0m1.774s\r\nuser\t0m0.430s\r\nsys\t0m1.370s\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -l  \"fentry:vmlinux:*\"  | wc -l\r\n48604\r\n\r\nreal\t0m0.449s\r\nuser\t0m0.288s\r\nsys\t0m0.193s\r\nroot@nano:~# time bpftrace -e  'fentry:vmlinux:schedule { print(comm) ; exit(0) }'\r\nAttached 1 probe\r\nkworker/u64:20\r\nkworker/u64:19\r\n\r\n\r\nreal\t0m0.743s\r\nuser\t0m0.304s\r\nsys\t0m0.207s\r\n```\r\nNote there are 2 less probes listed after the change, but is actually fix for incorrectly included probes before the change.\r\n\r\nUsers should not see any functional changes. \r\n\r\nTODO (in follow-up PR) : \r\n- write test(s) for lazy reading  \r\n- move  \"creating string streams out of function lists\" out of the `BPFtrace` class  to `ProbeMatcher`\r\n- propagate error up to inial caller i.e. `ProbeMatcher`\r\n- do not create unnecessary stream, just to check if traceable function set is not empty\r\n\r\n##### Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Language changes are updated in `docs/language.md`, `docs/stdlib.md`, or `man/adoc/bpftrace.adoc`\r\n- [ ] User-visible and non-trivial changes updated in `CHANGELOG.md`\r\n- [ ] The new behaviour is covered by tests\r\n\r\n",
      "reactions": {
