      },
      "body": "I've build a static bpftrace with alpine 3.10/llvm 8. On one host (debian buster with kernel 4.19) this works:\r\n\r\n```\r\nbpftrace -B line -e 'tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_open { printf(\"[%s] %s\\n\", comm, str(args->filename)); }'\r\n```\r\non another host (stretch, with kernel 4.19) the very same command fails with\r\n\r\n```\r\nlibclang: crash detected during parsing: {\r\n  'source_filename' : 'definitions.h'\r\n  'command_line_args' : ['clang', '-isystem', '/usr/local/include', '-isystem', '/bpftrace/include', '-isystem', '/usr/include', '-nostdinc', '-isystem', '/virtual/lib/clang/include', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/source/arch/x86/include', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/build/arch/x86/include/generated', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/source/include', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/build/include', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/source/arch/x86/include/uapi', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/build/arch/x86/include/generated/uapi', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/source/include/uapi', '-I/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/build/include/generated/uapi', '-include', '/lib/modules/4.19.0-0.bpo.5-amd64/source/include/linux/kconfig.h', '-D__KERNEL__', '-D__BPF_TRACING__', '-D__HAVE_BUILTIN_BSWAP16__', '-D__HAVE_BUILTIN_BSWAP32__', '-D__HAVE_BUILTIN_BSWAP64__', '-DKBUILD_MODNAME='\"bpftrace\"'', '-include', 'asm_goto_workaround.h'],\r\n  'unsaved_files' : [('definitions.h', '...', 263), ('/bpftrace/include/__stddef_max_align_t.h', '...', 1771), ('/bpftrace/include/float.h', '...', 5192), ('/bpftrace/include/limits.h', '...', 3735), ('/bpftrace/include/stdarg.h', '...', 2025), ('/bpftrace/include/stddef.h', '...', 4499), ('/bpftrace/include/stdint.h', '...', 23388), ('/bpftrace/include/asm_goto_workaround.h', '...', 667)],\r\n  'options' : 1,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut with this slight variation:\r\n\r\n```\r\nbpftrace -B line -e 'tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_open / 0 == 0 / { printf(\"[%s] %s\\n\", comm, str(args->filename)); }'\r\n```\r\n\r\nit works. I am wondering why this happends.",
