      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4593",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4593",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4593.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4593.patch",
        "merged_at": "2025-11-21T18:40:38Z"
      },
      "body": "<!--\r\nPlease provide a description of your change below this comment.\r\n\r\nThen please complete the checklist.\r\n\r\nUseful contribution guidelines and tips are in docs/developers.md.\r\n\r\nWarning: please make sure that you have implemented and tested your\r\n         change against the latest version of bpftrace (unless opening a\r\n         PR for a release branch).\r\n-->\r\n\r\nThis PR contains a related refactoring improvement aimed at improving code quality and consistency: USDT probe discovery mechanism migration: From BCC to libbpf ecosystem\r\n\r\nMajor Changes\r\nUSDT Probe Discovery Mechanism Refactoring (refactor: migrate USDT probe discovery from BCC to libbpf)\r\nBackground: Current codebase uses libbpf for USDT attachment but still relies on BCC APIs for probe discovery. This inconsistency increases maintenance complexity and dependency management overhead\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n✅ Add new ELF parser utility (src/util/elf_parser.{h,cpp}) for USDT probe enumeration\r\n✅ Implement USDTProbeEnumerator class with proper resource management (RAII)\r\n✅ Replace bcc_usdt_new_frompath/bcc_usdt_foreach with custom ELF parsing\r\n✅ Add support for .note.stapsdt section parsing and semaphore offset calculation\r\n✅ Unify codebase around libbpf ecosystem\r\n\r\n\r\nTechnical Details:\r\n* Uses libelf and gelf for native ELF file parsing\r\n* Supports USDT probe enumeration for both executables and shared libraries\r\n* Properly handles semaphore address to file offset conversion\r\n* Implements comprehensive error handling and resource management\r\n\r\n##### Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Language changes are updated in `docs/language.md`, `docs/stdlib.md`, or `man/adoc/bpftrace.adoc`\r\n- [ ] User-visible and non-trivial changes updated in `CHANGELOG.md`\r\n- [ ] The new behaviour is covered by tests\r\n",
      "reactions": {
