      "assignees": [

      ],
      "milestone": null,
      "comments": 3,
      "created_at": "2025-09-23T18:50:40Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-09-24T10:29:13Z",
      "closed_at": "2025-09-24T10:29:13Z",
      "assignee": null,
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": null,
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "sub_issues_summary": {
        "total": 0,
        "completed": 0,
        "percent_completed": 0
      },
      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "I feel like I'm taking crazy pills, but:\n```\n[ RUN      ] SemanticAnalyserTest.positional_parameters\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp:2961:3: runtime error: member call on null pointer of type 'struct PositionalParameter'\n    #0 0x560e957db521 in bpftrace::test::semantic_analyser::SemanticAnalyserTest_positional_parameters_Test::TestBody() (/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999_build/tests/bpftrace_test+0x90d521)\n    #1 0x7fe639c9d536 in void testing::internal::HandleExceptionsInMethodIfSupported<testing::Test, void>(testing::Test*, void (testing::Test::*)(), char const*) (/usr/lib64/libgtest.so.1.17.0+0x61536)\n```\nSo why does it succeed without ubsan? 🧐 \n```\ndiff --git a/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp b/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp\nindex 0a918907..0ef9219b 100644\n--- a/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp\n+++ b/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp\n@@ -2958,7 +2958,13 @@ TEST_F(SemanticAnalyserTest, positional_parameters)\n   auto *stmt =\n       ast.root->probes.at(0)->block->stmts.at(0).as<ast::ExprStatement>();\n   auto *pp = stmt->expr.as<ast::PositionalParameter>();\n-  EXPECT_EQ(CreateNone(), pp->type());\n+  std::printf(\"--> pp: %p\\n\", pp);\n+  std::printf(\"--> pp->type: %ld\\n\", pp->type());\n+\n+  SizedType none = CreateNone();\n+  std::printf(\"--> none: %ld\\n\", none);\n+\n+  EXPECT_EQ(none, pp->type());\n \n   bpftrace->add_param(\"0999\");\n   test(\"kprobe:f { printf(\\\"%d\\\", $4); }\", Mock{ *bpftrace }, Error{});\n```\nsez:\n```\n[ RUN      ] SemanticAnalyserTest.positional_parameters\n--> pp: (nil)\n--> pp->type: 140733877583008\n--> none: 140733877583008\n[       OK ] SemanticAnalyserTest.positional_parameters (493 ms)\n```\nEqual, all right..as expected.\n\nBut wait: why is `stmt->expr.as<ast::PositionalParameter>()` returning a `nullptr` (instead of an empty whatever) and more importantly why is dereferencing that `nullptr` now a thing? 😭 \n\nLooking at [the code](https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/blob/master/src/ast/ast.h#L305) the only explanation I can come up with is that ->type() returning a static is so const and super inlined that the referent `pp` does not matter..or something.\n\nI swear I don't want to be difficult with all these issues but this is crazytown!\nFortunately this is the last UBSan complaint found so far.\n",
