      },
      "body": "Hello\r\nI am trying to do a static build of bpftrace, but failing to find `libclang.a`\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DSTATIC_LINKING:BOOL=ON ../\r\n$ make\r\n/usr/bin/ld: cannot find -lclang\r\ncollect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status\r\nsrc/CMakeFiles/bpftrace.dir/build.make:566: recipe for target 'src/bpftrace' failed\r\nmake[2]: *** [src/bpftrace] Error 1\r\nCMakeFiles/Makefile2:236: recipe for target 'src/CMakeFiles/bpftrace.dir/all' failed\r\nmake[1]: *** [src/CMakeFiles/bpftrace.dir/all] Error 2\r\nMakefile:140: recipe for target 'all' failed\r\nmake: *** [all] Error 2\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ sudo /usr/share/bcc/tools/opensnoop -x -n ld\r\nPID    COMM               FD ERR PATH\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7/../../../../lib/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /lib/../lib/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /usr/lib/../lib/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7/../../../libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/local/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu64/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/local/lib64/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //lib64/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/lib64/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/local/lib/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //lib/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/lib/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/x86_64-linux-gnu/lib64/libclang.a\r\n8756   ld                 -1   2 //usr/x86_64-linux-gnu/lib/libclang.a\r\n```\r\n\r\nI checked on ubuntu's repositories and `libclang.a` is not provided, I even downloaded the 7.0.1 release of clang and the file is also not in the tar.. where am I supposed to get it?\r\n\r\nJust as sanity check - I am running the exact same commands that the ubuntu docker image is running..",
