      "node_id": "PR_kwDOCMCh9c6l3L-D",
      "number": 4513,
      "title": "build: remove `libbpf/bpf.h` and namespace guard",
      "user": {
        "login": "amscanne",
        "id": 425773,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTc3Mw==",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/425773?v=4",
        "gravatar_id": "",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/amscanne",
        "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/followers",
        "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/following{/other_user}",
        "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/gists{/gist_id}",
        "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
        "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/subscriptions",
        "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/orgs",
        "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/repos",
        "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/events{/privacy}",
        "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/amscanne/received_events",
        "type": "User",
        "user_view_type": "public",
        "site_admin": false
      },
      "labels": [

      ],
      "state": "closed",
      "locked": false,
      "assignees": [

      ],
      "milestone": null,
      "comments": 0,
      "created_at": "2025-08-28T19:02:04Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-09-02T16:11:27Z",
      "closed_at": "2025-09-02T16:11:25Z",
      "assignee": null,
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": null,
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "draft": false,
      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4513",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4513",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4513.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4513.patch",
        "merged_at": "2025-09-02T16:11:25Z"
      },
      "body": "Stacked PRs:\n * #4516\n * __->__#4513\n\n\n--- --- ---\n\n### build: remove `libbpf/bpf.h` and namespace guard\n\n\nSince `libbpf` is a static dependency, it makes little sense to have a\nmanually curated vendored header as well.\n\nUnfortunately, the use of this header is a bit of a mess. Since it\nincludes the lovely `#pragma once`, it will only be included once.\nUnfortunately, our poor header hygiene means that in some places this\nheader was included in a namespace guard (e.g. putting all those types\ninto a `libbpf` namespace), and in other cases not.\n\nOne option might be to guard this header everywhere it is used, but\nthere are two major problems with this:\n\n* This quickly becomes a pain if we actually do have IWYU hygiene, and\n  include the header in files where these details are needed.\n\n* Other libraries may need `libbpf` types, and putting them into a\n  special namespace when we include them first breaks their use\n  elsewhere. (Also applies to the case where these namespaced headers\n  are including anything else. This is why it's a bad idea to have\n  `#include` inside any namespace.)\n\nThe best approach here is to simply leave those types in the global\nnamespace (since it is a C library, after all), and try to introduce\nsensible types and wrappers locally to minimize the need to exercise\nthat API surface. If we really want a `libbpf` namespace, then we should\ndo a proper C++ libbpf, rather than inconsistently loading that header\nin a namespace.\n\nSigned-off-by: Adin Scannell <amscanne@meta.com>\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4513/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
