      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "draft": false,
      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/pulls/4799",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4799",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4799.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4799.patch",
        "merged_at": "2025-11-01T11:49:09Z"
      },
      "body": "linux >= v6.1 support bpf_task_from_pid/bpf_task_release kfuncs, this patch use these kfuncs to stdlib, and apply them to macros.\r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n\r\n    $ kill -CHLD {1,2,3,4,5,6}\r\n\r\n    $ sudo ./killsnoop.bt\r\n    Attached 8 probes\r\n    Tracing kill(),tkill(),tgkill() signals... Hit Ctrl-C to end.\r\n    TIME                 PID COMM                    SIG     TPID TCOMM            RESULT\r\n    19:04:24.343503     4588 bash                SIGCHLD        1 systemd              -1\r\n    19:04:24.343562     4588 bash                SIGCHLD        2 kthreadd             -1\r\n    19:04:24.343577     4588 bash                SIGCHLD        3 pool_workqueue_      -1\r\n    19:04:24.343588     4588 bash                SIGCHLD        4 kworker/R-rcu_g      -1\r\n    19:04:24.343600     4588 bash                SIGCHLD        5 kworker/R-sync_      -1\r\n    19:04:24.343611     4588 bash                SIGCHLD        6 kworker/R-kvfre      -1\r\n\r\nThis patch is the second attempt to introduce bpf_task_from_pid/bpf_task_release. the first was in [1].\r\n\r\nLink: https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/pull/4197 [1]\r\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4799/reactions",
