      "assignees": [

      ],
      "milestone": null,
      "comments": 11,
      "created_at": "2025-10-09T22:58:22Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-10-15T07:45:05Z",
      "closed_at": "2025-10-15T07:45:05Z",
      "assignee": null,
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": null,
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "sub_issues_summary": {
        "total": 0,
        "completed": 0,
        "percent_completed": 0
      },
      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "### What reproduces the bug? Provide code if possible.\n\n```\n# bpftrace -e 'tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_* { print(probe); exit() }'\ndefinitions.h:1946:33: error: field has incomplete type 'const enum landlock_rule_type'\ndefinitions.h:1946:14: note: forward declaration of 'enum landlock_rule_type'\nClang parse error\n```\nIn particular it seems to be caused by sys_enter_landlock_add_rule (as guessed from the error), e.g. for faster test:\n```\nbpftrace -e 'tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_landlock_add_rule {} BEGIN { exit() }'\n```\n\n\nFirst noticed on nixos test VM when updating to v0.24.1 from v0.23.5, but it reproduces just fine on a fedora host and I've bisected it down to these two commits (fails to build with just one; the three commits in the middle have been tested individually and are fine):\n- 813f5714f506 cleanup: remove `tp_args_struct_level`\n- 2b0a0f53032e Remove references to tp_args_structs_level\n\nI tried reverting on master but src/tracepoint_format_parser.cpp changed quite a bit after these commits so I didn't push through; hopefully someone will figure this out better than me.\n\n### `bpftrace --info` output\n\n```\nSystem\n  OS: Linux 6.15.10-200.fc42.x86_64 #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri Aug 15 15:57:06 UTC 2025\n  Arch: x86_64\n\nBuild\n  version: v0.21.0-653-g2b0a\n  LLVM: 20.1.8\n  bfd: yes\n  libdw (DWARF support): yes\n  libsystemd (systemd notify support): no\n\nKernel helpers\n  probe_read: yes                  probe_read_str: yes                \n  probe_read_user: yes             probe_read_user_str: yes           \n  probe_read_kernel: yes           probe_read_kernel_str: yes         \n  get_current_cgroup_id: yes       send_signal: yes                   \n  override_return: no              get_boot_ns: yes                   \n  dpath: yes                       skboutput: yes                     \n  get_tai_ns: yes                  get_func_ip: yes                   \n  jiffies64: yes                   for_each_map_elem: yes             \n  get_ns_current_pid_tgid: yes     lookup_percpu_elem: yes            \n\nKernel features\n  Instruction limit: 1000000       btf: yes                           \n  module btf: yes                  map batch: yes                     \n  uprobe refcount: yes             \n\nMap types                          \n  hash: yes                        array: yes                         \n  percpu array: yes                stack_trace: yes                   \n  perf_event_array: yes            ringbuf: yes                       \n\nProbe types\n  kprobe: yes                      tracepoint: yes                    \n  perf_event: yes                  fentry: yes                        \n  kprobe_multi: yes                uprobe_multi: no                   \n  kprobe_session: yes              iter: yes                          \n```\n",
