      "body": "Followup to #4566.\n\nUnfortunately building with LTO is still problematic.\n\n1) due to an inevitable inconsistency between `src/libbpf/bpf.h` and the system libbpf's `bpf.h`:\n```\n[661/662] : && /usr/lib/ccache/bin/x86_64-pc-linux-gnu-g++ -pipe -O2 -march=znver2 -fno-semantic-interposition -flto=8 -fuse-linker-plugin -Wl,-O1,--as-needed,-z,now,-z,pack-relative-relocs -flto=8 -fuse-linker-plugin -Wl,--dependency-file=tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/link.d tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/arch.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/async_action.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/bpfbytecode.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/bpftrace.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/btf.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/child.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/clang_parser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/named_param.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/config.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/collect_nodes.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/deprecated.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/field_analyser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/fold_literals.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/function_registry.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/globalvars.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/imports.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/location.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/log.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/macro_expansion.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/main.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/memfd.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/mocks.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/opaque.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/output.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/parser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/portability_analyser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/probe_expansion.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/procmon.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/probe.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/config_analyser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/pass_manager.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/pid_filter_pass.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/recursion_check.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/resource_analyser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/result.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/required_resources.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/return_path_analyser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/scopeguard.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/semantic_analyser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/temp.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/tracepoint_format_parser.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/types.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/type_system.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/unstable_feature.cpp.o tests/CMakeFiles/bpftrace_test.dir/utils.cpp.o -o tests/bpftrace_test  -Wl,-rpath,/usr/lib/llvm/21/lib64  src/libbpftrace.a  src/btf/libbtf.a  /usr/lib64/libgtest_main.so.1.17.0  /usr/lib64/libgmock.so  src/libruntime.a  /usr/lib64/libblazesym_c.so  src/output/liboutput.a  /usr/lib64/libbpf.so  /usr/lib64/libbfd.so  /usr/lib64/libopcodes.so  /usr/lib64/libbcc_bpf.so  /usr/lib64/libdw.so  src/aot/libaot.a  src/librequired_resources.a  src/ast/libast.a  src/btf/libbtf.a  libparser.a  src/tracefs/libtracefs.a  src/stdlib/libstdlib.a  src/ast/libast_defs.a  src/libcompiler_core.a  /usr/lib/llvm/21/lib64/libclang.so.21.1.1  /usr/lib/llvm/21/lib64/libclang-cpp.so.21.1  /usr/lib/llvm/21/lib64/libLLVM.so.21.1  src/arch/libarch.a  src/util/libutil.a  src/debugfs/libdebugfs.a  /usr/lib64/libz.so  /usr/lib64/libelf.so  src/cxxdemangler/libcxxdemangler_llvm.a  /usr/lib64/libgtest.so.1.17.0 && :\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/src/libbpf/bpf.h:20:6: warning: type 'bpf_map_type' violates the C++ One Definition Rule [-Wodr]\n   20 | enum bpf_map_type {\n      |      ^\n/usr/include/linux/bpf.h:967:6: note: an enum with different value name is defined in another translation unit\n  967 | enum bpf_map_type {\n      |      ^\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/src/libbpf/bpf.h:40:9: note: name 'BPF_MAP_TYPE_CGROUP_STORAGE' differs from name 'BPF_MAP_TYPE_CGROUP_STORAGE_DEPRECATED' defined in another translation unit\n   40 |         BPF_MAP_TYPE_CGROUP_STORAGE,\n      |         ^\n/usr/include/linux/bpf.h:987:9: note: mismatching definition\n  987 |         BPF_MAP_TYPE_CGROUP_STORAGE_DEPRECATED,\n      |         ^\n>>> Source compiled.\n```\n\nHowever this seems benign (for now), at least for our purposes and the following points.\n\n2) failures in `SemanticAnalyserTest.uprobe` and `.probe_short_name`:\n```\n[ RUN      ] SemanticAnalyserTest.uprobe\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp:180: Failure\nExpected equality of these values:\n  errstr\n    Which is: \"stdin:1:1-12: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\\nuprobe:sh:f { 1 }\\n~~~~~~~~~~~\\n\"\n  \"\"\nWith diff:\n@@ -1,3 +1,1 @@\n-stdin:1:1-12: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\n-uprobe:sh:f { 1 }\n-~~~~~~~~~~~\\n\n+\"\"\n\nstdin:1:1-12: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\nuprobe:sh:f { 1 }\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp:180: Failure\nExpected equality of these values:\n  errstr\n    Which is: \"stdin:1:1-15: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\\nuretprobe:sh:f { 1 }\\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\\n\"\n  \"\"\nWith diff:\n@@ -1,3 +1,1 @@\n-stdin:1:1-15: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\n-uretprobe:sh:f { 1 }\n-~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\\n\n+\"\"\n\nstdin:1:1-15: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\nuretprobe:sh:f { 1 }\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp:180: Failure\nExpected equality of these values:\n  errstr\n    Which is: \"stdin:1:1-8: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\\nur:sh:f { 1 }\\n~~~~~~~\\n\"\n  \"\"\nWith diff:\n@@ -1,3 +1,1 @@\n-stdin:1:1-8: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\n-ur:sh:f { 1 }\n-~~~~~~~\\n\n+\"\"\n\nstdin:1:1-8: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\nur:sh:f { 1 }\n~~~~~~~\n\n\n[  FAILED  ] SemanticAnalyserTest.uprobe (406 ms)\n```\n...\n```\n[       OK ] SemanticAnalyserTest.per_cpu_map_as_map_key (177 ms)\n[ RUN      ] SemanticAnalyserTest.probe_short_name\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp:180: Failure\nExpected equality of these values:\n  errstr\n    Which is: \"stdin:1:1-7: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\\nu:sh:f { 1 }\\n~~~~~~\\n\"\n  \"\"\nWith diff:\n@@ -1,3 +1,1 @@\n-stdin:1:1-7: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\n-u:sh:f { 1 }\n-~~~~~~\\n\n+\"\"\n\nstdin:1:1-7: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\nu:sh:f { 1 }\n~~~~~~\n\n\n/tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/tests/semantic_analyser.cpp:180: Failure\nExpected equality of these values:\n  errstr\n    Which is: \"stdin:1:1-8: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\\nur:sh:f { 1 }\\n~~~~~~~\\n\"\n  \"\"\nWith diff:\n@@ -1,3 +1,1 @@\n-stdin:1:1-8: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\n-ur:sh:f { 1 }\n-~~~~~~~\\n\n+\"\"\n\nstdin:1:1-8: ERROR: uprobe target file 'sh' does not exist or is not executable\nur:sh:f { 1 }\n~~~~~~~\n\n\n[  FAILED  ] SemanticAnalyserTest.probe_short_name (173 ms)\n```\nBoth of these seem to be related to expected output comparison, but why do they only happen with LTO? Also see the section below why these failures are weird.\n\n3) the unit tests crash in `childproc.multi_exec_match`:\n```\n[       OK ] childproc.ptrace_child_term_before_execve (10 ms)\n[ RUN      ] childproc.multi_exec_match\nzsh: segmentation fault  ./bpftrace_test\n```\nor when run in gdb:\n```\n[       OK ] childproc.ptrace_child_term_before_execve (11 ms)\n[ RUN      ] childproc.multi_exec_match\n[Detaching after fork from child process 4793]\n\nThread 1 \"bpftrace_test\" received signal SIGSEGV, Segmentation fault.\n0x00007fffea573fd9 in __strlen_avx2 () from /lib64/libc.so.6\n(gdb) bt full\n#0  0x00007fffea573fd9 in __strlen_avx2 () from /lib64/libc.so.6\nNo symbol table info available.\n#1  0x00007fffea4475da in __add_to_environ () from /lib64/libc.so.6\nNo symbol table info available.\n#2  0x00005555557b4d12 in bpftrace::test::child::childproc_multi_exec_match_Test::TestBody (this=0x7fffe007d750)\n    at /tmp/portage/dev-debug/bpftrace-0.24.9999/work/bpftrace-0.24.9999/tests/child.cpp:271\n        gtest_ar = {success_ = true, message_ = std::unique_ptr<std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char> >> = {get() = 0x0}}\n        ec = std::error_code = {std::_V2::error_category: 0}\n        tmpdir = \"/tmp/bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u\"\n        path = filesystem::path \"/tmp/bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u\" = {[root-directory] = \"/\", [1] = \"tmp\", [2] = \"bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u\"}\n        usr_bin = filesystem::path \"/tmp/bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u/usr/bin\" = {[root-directory] = \"/\", [1] = \"tmp\", [2] = \"bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u\", [3] = \"usr\", [4] = \"bin\"}\n        symlink_bin = filesystem::path \"/tmp/bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u/bin\" = {[root-directory] = \"/\", [1] = \"tmp\", [2] = \"bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u\", [3] = \"bin\"}\n        binary = filesystem::path \"/tmp/bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u/usr/bin/mysleep\" = {[root-directory] = \"/\", [1] = \"tmp\", [2] = \"bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u\", [3] = \"usr\", \n          [4] = \"bin\", [5] = \"mysleep\"}\n        old_path = 0x0\n        new_path = \"/tmp/bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u/usr/bin:/tmp/bpftrace-test-child-9ayf2u/bin\"\n        child = std::unique_ptr<bpftrace::ChildProc> = {get() = 0x5555565f1b80}\n#3  0x00007ffff13ca537 in void testing::internal::HandleExceptionsInMethodIfSupported<testing::Test, void>(testing::Test*, void (testing::Test::*)(), char const*) ()\n   from /usr/lib64/libgtest.so.1.17.0\n```\n\n### The weird part\n\nOddly enough issues 2 and 3 only seem to happen when running the full test (`./bpftrace_test`), **not** when running only the affected tests e.g. via `./bpftrace_test --gtest_filter=childproc.* --gtest_repeat=10 --gtest_shuffle` (or `--gtest_filter=SemanticAnalyserTest.*`). This smells like some kind of internal corruption to me.\n\n### What reproduces the bug? Provide code if possible.\n\nBuild with LTO & run the unit tests.\n",
