      "issue_field_values": [

      ],
      "type": {
        "id": 82711,
        "node_id": "IT_kwDOCWTeF84AAUMX",
        "name": "Task",
        "description": "A specific piece of work",
        "color": "yellow",
        "created_at": "2024-01-24T13:01:17Z",
        "updated_at": "2024-07-26T10:04:48Z",
        "is_enabled": true
      },
      "active_lock_reason": null,
      "sub_issues_summary": {
        "total": 0,
        "completed": 0,
        "percent_completed": 0
      },
      "parent_issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4144",
      "issue_dependencies_summary": {
        "blocked_by": 0,
        "total_blocked_by": 0,
        "blocking": 0,
        "total_blocking": 0
      },
      "body": "`AttachedProbe::attach_usdt()` uses bcc's `bpf_attach_uprobe()` to attach usdt probes (which are actually just backed by uprobes). This can be migrated to libbpf's `bpf_program__attach_uprobe()`.\n\nNote that `attach_usdt()` makes use of a few other bcc APIs. This issue does not intend to migrate those usages to libbpf ones. That task would be much harder. It should be doable, though. We'll eventually do it, but sooner is better than later. Many bonus points if you can figure that out. This might need to be done in sync with other parts of the codebase like codegen.\n",
      "reactions": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bpftrace/bpftrace/issues/4151/reactions",
        "total_count": 0,
        "+1": 0,
        "-1": 0,
